00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:23.440
I am describing a tool, not selling one. If you only change one setting this week, make it that 20-day volume column.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.620
Quiet names fail the first test before you waste a minute on the rest.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:40.900
World Liberty Financial's Trust Company received preliminary approval from the office of the Comptroller of the Currency, or OCC, which is the first formal step toward that Trump family crypto venture becoming a national bank.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:51.120
That kind of regulatory foothold can accelerate institutional custody flows into approved vehicles, but it is not a buy the headline signal on Bitcoin itself.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:10:04.420
The action is narrow. Add a 1-2% position in a regulated Bitcoin exchange traded fund, or ETF, only after it closes above its 50-day moving average on above average volume.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:17.720
Separately, Northwestern Mutual found that 42% of Americans now report relying on the previous generation for support, and the study treats that rate as a structural feature, not a leftover from the pandemic.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:27.240
Sustain demand for income generating assets among younger cohorts can keep high yield utility names well supported for longer than a typical cycle trade.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:36.920
If you already hold utilities inside a TFSA, reviewed dividend coverage and only consider ads where coverage sits above 1.5 times.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:46.100
Across 50 simulated trades, the portfolio shows a 56% wind rate and accumulative profit of $333.39.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:11:01.760
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ composite stands at plus 9.28% across 45 verified window trades, while the buy and hold gap versus the same index remains minus 18.79% since inception.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:15.160
That running total is 28 winning trades against 21 losses and 1 break even, with the largest single gain at plus 20.11%, and the largest loss at minus 11.8%.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:26.840
The matched window measure compares each $1,000 position only against the NASDAQ return over its exact holding period, so we are not pretending a single name book is a fully invested index.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:35.980
The book is learning the volume confirmation pattern the hard way and adjusting the next entry, which is why today's watch list is a watch list, not a fill.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:44.440
Now, here is something that most retail investors get wrong, and it cost me real allocation years before I had language for it.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:56.540
Imagine you opened a TFS a last year and put 40% into TSX financials and energy names, because the dividend tax credit felt familiar and the currency hedge felt comforting.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:03.440
The bid asks spreads on those large caps stayed tight, so nothing about the trading experience warned you.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:10.620
The portfolio still moved almost in lockstep with oil prices and bank earnings revisions, instead of global growth.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:21.300
Canada is roughly 3% of global market capitalization. Many Canadian investors still hold 30% to 50% of their equity allocation in TSX stocks.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:38.060
What gets missed is that your salary, your home, and your Canada pension plan, or CPP, already embed heavy domestic exposure, so another 30% to 50% in TSX names effectively doubles the bet on a 3% slice of world market cap.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:47.980
Professionals run a geographic breakdown first. They check the MSCI all-country world indexed country weights before they touch another Canadian name.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:54.500
Then they cap home bias at 20% to 25%, unless a specific valuation gap shows up.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:13:02.660
The case for home bias is real, the dividend tax credit, the built-in currency hedge, and the simple fact that you know the companies.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:17.700
The case against is heavier than most kitchen table portfolios admit. Financials and energy together make up about half the TSX, and the index is missing the global tech and healthcare leaders that have driven much of the recent NASDAQ performance.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:23.760
The misconception is treating familiarity as diversification. The fix is concrete.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:33.140
Calculate your true Canada weight across every account once a quarter, and rebalance any excess into a low-cost global X Canada ETF.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:46.740
That same allocation discipline is why Loon.TO, even as a TSX name we are watching, does not get a free pass into the simulated book just because it is local and the buyback sounds friendly.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:14:01.260
Before we wrap, add Loon.TO to your watch list tonight. Set an alert at the 50-day moving average, and write down today's 20-day average volume so you can see whether any bounce actually clears it at Mondays open.

